THE PAPER. 22 pages. A sliding block code from Zeckendorf folding, with two sharp thresholds.

For each m the length-m Fibonacci fold induces a sliding block code from the full two-sided binary shift onto a sofic image. The paper proves it is a topological conjugacy for every m >= 3, and locates two different sharp thresholds. Whole-block reconstruction: m consecutive labels determine the entire length-(2m-1) lift, and at length 2m-2 distinct blocks share a folded-window sequence. Local decoding: three consecutive labels determine the current raw digit and two do not, so the exact zero-anticipation memory of the inverse is 2, independent of m, despite the unbounded carry cascades of Fibonacci normalization. The mechanism is a four-state carry graph and a boundary cancellation identity. At m = 2 the only failure of injectivity is that the two fixed points share an image. I verified both thresholds exhaustively, including at m = 9 over all 131072 words, and both witness families reproduce.

